# CITATION.cff: how to cite AgentProof (https://citation-file-format.github.io/)
# Only verified facts are recorded. There is deliberately NO doi, orcid, publication or registration number:
# none exists yet. Add them here only after you actually obtain them (see docs/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AgentProof in research or when evaluating an agent, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "AgentProof: chaos testing, state-based grading and replay for AI agents"
abstract: >-
  AgentProof is a zero-dependency Python harness for evaluating AI agents that take real actions.
  It injects production-style tool failures, grades the final state of a simulated world instead of
  the transcript, records every run so failures can be replayed, and provides a CI reliability gate.
  It also includes a bitemporal memory module with provenance and a calibrated human-in-the-loop router.
